      "writtenOn": "2023-09-15T03:42:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could you send CMD_BASE_SERVING_ERROR in the async case too, or is that too dangerous a change ? It would make the async and sync cases closer together.\n\nIf you don\u0027t think this is safe, then keep your current code and add some comments in this method explaining what this is doing, e.g.\n\n    // There was an error and the state machine should return to the initial\n    // state. For the sync state machine, this is accomplished by sending a\n    // self message which will be processed after this message processing is\n    // complete (so before the control is given back to the caller).\n    // For the async state machine, transitionTo() imposes an async round trip.\n    // Sending the same message as with the sync case would impose 2 round\n    // trips, which is a departure from legacy code so keep closer to the\n    // legacy code for now.",
